# =============================================================================
# Deterministic checkout behavior — prevents the recurring cPanel Git
# "uncommitted changes on the checked-out branch" deploy block.
#
# WHY: on a fresh clone, git can renormalize line endings differently on the
# shared host than on a dev machine (depending on the host's core.autocrlf).
# Any tracked file whose EOLs get rewritten then shows as "modified", dirtying
# the working tree and blocking the next deploy. Pinning EOL policy here — a
# COMMITTED file that travels with the repo, unlike .git/config — stops that.
# =============================================================================

# Do not touch line endings on ANY file: whatever is committed is what is
# checked out, byte-for-byte, on every machine including the host. This is the
# safest choice for a repo that commits `vendor/` (which contains files with
# mixed/CRLF endings we must not rewrite).
* -text

# Treat everything as binary for diff/merge purposes too where endings matter,
# by being explicit about the vendored assets that ship with CRLF.
*.map -text
